A||||12||Black88GT||Performance fuel setup, overkill???||||1||
Z||000000||Black88GT||01-09-2001||08:46 PM||||I was thinking of buying a 255lph Fuel Pump from Summit and finally using the 19# injectors I forgot about when doing the swap.  I have a 3.4 right now with stock fuel pump and stock 2.8 injectors.  Do you think the 255 lph fuel pump is overkill?  Everything is stock on the car except for the exhaust (borla/no cat) and manifolds (ported).<P>I heard that the car will run rich with this setup, but I can rememdy that with Joe Wynmans chip...<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||01-09-2001||10:10 PM||||If your stock pump and fuel injectors are giving you the correct air fuel ratios throughout the rpm band than you are not going to see an improvement in power. <P>The 3.4-liter Camaro engine does run rich with 19 lb. hour fuel injectors and you will need a custom prom made up for you to make them work. <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||01-10-2001||08:00 AM||||I thought the stock injectors were 19#?  <P>I know about the chip, thats why I mentioned Joe Wynman.  He sells it for $100 plus shipping||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||01-10-2001||08:23 AM||||ask GT Bastard... he's got 55# at 110psi  <A HREF="http://www.rceng.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rceng.com</A>  (about 36# at 42psi - Thanks BBBad GT) with a 240gph pump from an 87 Iroc-Z. it's KICKS serious @$$ and was great for nitrous! it doens't run too rich. <P>(has custom chip from Custom Network Motors but a plain ADS Strip chip would run it ok to...) <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Will||01-10-2001||09:34 AM||||How much does that pump from Summit cost?<BR>A '96(?) Corvette fuel pump is a plug in swap for the Fiero pump, costs about $80 from the dealership, and will supply as much fuel as a 3.4 would ever need.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroSTETZ||01-10-2001||12:33 PM||||how bout the bigger injectors and pump, then getting the dual throttle bodies from fieroshop (manifold w/ throttle body on both ends) says you need a richer mixture to use it...||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||01-10-2001||05:05 PM||||I thought the stock fiero fuel injectors were 16 lb. injectors. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Black88GT||01-10-2001||08:54 PM||||I thought stock Fiero injectors were 15 and the 3.4 was 19.  Now you guys got me second guessing myself! Oh well, I am sure someone knows.  I could have sworn they were 19 though.<P>The Fuel pump from Summit is made by Granatelli motorsports, it was recommended to me by HYPTNOTiSE, it sells for like 120 I think plus shipping.  Whats the flow rate of the corvette pump?  Sounds very tempting...<P>I didn't know the Fiero shop had dual TB setup.  Last I heard Chris West was working on it, but thats been like forever now.  How much is the one from the Fiero shop???<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000008||Black88GT||01-11-2001||03:09 PM||||anyone?||||reg||5
Z||000009||Will||01-11-2001||03:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B><BR>The Fuel pump from Summit is made by Granatelli motorsports, it was recommended to me by HYPTNOTiSE, it sells for like 120 I think plus shipping.  Whats the flow rate of the corvette pump?  Sounds very tempting...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't know the flow rate, but that is the same pump used with the 330 HP LT4 engine. That engine was a '96 only Corvette only option and was the same thing to the LT1 that the LS6 is to the LS1.<BR>Anyway, that pump will probably supply 400 HP worth of fuel.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Alex4mula||01-11-2001||04:44 PM||||If you can't flow more air then you won't need more fuel. My 3.4 (stock 2.8 inj. , FPR, headers & ported everything)feels stronger lean than when rich.  If it is running Ok now then why spend $$ on it? I would measure A/F ratio first before spending that $$. Unless you plan on Nitro, turbo, etc. in future...||||reg||1
Z||000011||Black88GT||01-11-2001||04:53 PM||||I was considering turbo in the summer. Also I heard the Fiero shop sells dual TB, figure that would help with Air Flow, if I don't get the turbo. <P>No one knows what the 3.4 injectors are?  I am pretty sure they are 19# but I need some confirmation before I change my stock 2.8 injectors....<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000012||88formula||01-11-2001||05:19 PM||||Read somewhere that the 3.4 injectors are 21 lb. and hour.||||reg||1
